 summarzie

▾ Thought for 7s
  Frontend discrepancies in manual refund method slugs were causing 422 errors. The frontend selection values were
  updated to align precisely with backend database slugs. This synchronization aims to resolve the mismatch that was
  triggering the error.


  Removed the legacy buttons causing 422 errors and consolidated them into a unified offline refund flow, preventing
  redundant manual interventions. Identified and corrected icon errors in the Angular templates, ensuring the display o
  valid icons. Improved status displays across the interface to clarify the various refund and payment states to the
  user.

  Adjusted backend transaction handling to prevent database rollbacks of refund status upon conflict detection,
  ensuring data persistence. Enhanced gateway synchronization to support various refund states, specifically
  synchronizing bookings to "REFUNDED" status upon full refund settlement and blocking duplicate payout attempts.
  ### Summary of Completed Work
  ──────
  ### 1. UI & Admin Drawer Fixes

  • Manual Refund Method Slugs: Fixed frontend dropdown values (bank, gpay, razorpay_dashboard, cash, other) to match
  backend validation, eliminating 422 Unprocessable Entity errors when recording manual payouts.
  • Deprecated Support Actions Removed: Cleaned up obsolete drawer buttons (Mark refund pending and Mark payment
  resolved manually), streamlining the drawer into the single "Record Offline Refund" flow.
  • Icon & Template Corrections: Resolved Angular template icon errors in fixed-departures.component.ts to keep the
  frontend compilation clean.
  ──────
  ### 2. Backend & Gateway Synchronization Fixes

  • Database Rollback Bug: In AdminFixedDeparturesController.php:286, removed the outer DB::transaction wrapper
  around manual refund recording. When Razorpay already refunded a customer, the 409 conflict now permanently
  persists the synced REFUNDED status rather than rolling it back to APPROVED.
  • Repeated Partial Refund Deductions: In RefundRegisterService.php:158, partial refund balances are now computed
  against the immutable base fare. Re-verifying a ₹20 partial refund on a ₹120 booking consistently preserves the
  ₹100 remaining balance without deducting ₹20 again on repeated attempts.
  • Pending vs. Partial Priority: In RazorpayService.php:271, any in-flight pending gateway refund (e.g. ₹20
  processed + ₹100 pending) takes priority, transitioning the booking to REQUESTED (Refund pending confirmation) and
  blocking duplicate offline payouts.
  • Safe Gateway Verification Failure: When Razorpay is unreachable or network calls fail, RazorpayService.php:340
  flags the state as unverified and returns a 503 error. The system halts safely and leaves the booking as APPROVED
  instead of assuming 0 refunds.
  ──────
  ### 3. Verification & Test Results

   Test Suite                            |          Tests          |       Assertions       |         Status
  ---------------------------------------|-------------------------|------------------------|------------------------
   FixedAdminRecoveryActionsTest.php     |           14            |          106           |     PASSED (100%)
   DoubleRefundPreventionTest.php        |            6            |           31           |     PASSED (100%)
   Frontend Typecheck (npx tsc --noEmit) |            —            |           —            |        0 Errors